---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SectionHead from '~/components/SectionHead.astro'
import Logo from '~/components/Logo.astro'
import { SITE } from '~/data/site'

const principles = [
  {
    name: 'The publisher owns the content, the profile and the frontend.',
    body: 'Konneal builds the databases and serves the API.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Every release is measured.',
    body: 'A golden question set with expected citations runs three times before any change is promoted.',
  },
  {
    name: 'The models are open-weight.',
    body: 'No corpus data is sent to third-party services, and no part of the system depends on a proprietary model provider.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Citations open the original document.',
    body: 'Every answer names the publication, edition and clause behind it, and the citation opens the original document at that clause.',
  },
]
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Konneal is the serving layer of a suite in which standards are authored in Metanorma, modelled in Primmel, and served by Konneal."
>
  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-12 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-16">
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-sans text-[2.1rem] font-semibold leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.01em] sm:text-[2.7rem]">
        About Konneal
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Standards are authored in Metanorma, modelled in Primmel, and served by Konneal. Konneal runs annealment
        passes over a corpus the organization has already authored, and turns it into a question-answering service
        whose every answer carries its own evidence — and whose rules are executed, with the arithmetic shown.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.3fr)_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        <div>
          <SectionHead title="Where the name comes from" />
          <ol class="mt-8 space-y-6">
            <li class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-[3.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
              <p class="font-mono text-[0.85rem] font-medium text-blue">01</p>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-sans text-[1.05rem] font-semibold">K-onneal — knowledge annealment</h3>
                <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
                  The method itself: repeated passes that add verified structure to a corpus, each pass leaving a
                  record. The full definition is on
                  <a href="/annealment/" class="text-blue underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-keyline"
                    >the annealment page</a
                  >.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-[3.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
              <p class="font-mono text-[0.85rem] font-medium text-blue">02</p>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-sans text-[1.05rem] font-semibold">Anneal — the metallurgy</h3>
                <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
                  Heat treatment that hardens metal into a durable structure: soft becomes durable, prose becomes
                  computable.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-[3.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
              <p class="font-mono text-[0.85rem] font-medium text-blue">03</p>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-sans text-[1.05rem] font-semibold">Konne(ction) — the joins</h3>
                <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
                  The organization connects to its members, questions connect to clauses, answers connect to the
                  original document.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-start justify-center gap-8 border border-rule bg-surface p-10">
          <Logo variant="light" lockup="primary" />
          <p class="text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            The mark is the suite in miniature: three layered sheared slabs — structure being added to structure, each
            layer locked to the same shear. Authored, modelled, served.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <SectionHead title="From a live service to a product" />
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        <p>
          Konneal was born from a live public service. The engine began as the serving layer of a deployed,
          publicly testable question-answering service over a real standards corpus, and was extracted into this
          publisher-agnostic product with its history preserved — the same retrieval, the same answer contract, the
          same verdict engine, and the same gates.
        </p>
        <p>
          The method was not designed on a whiteboard; it was measured into existence. The annealment ladder and its
          staircase are the recorded result of grading the same questions over successively richer representations of
          the same corpus.
        </p>
        <p>
          Konneal is developed by
          <a href={SITE.company.url} class="text-blue underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-keyline" rel="noopener"
            >{SITE.company.name}</a
          >, alongside the rest of the suite.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <SectionHead title="How we work" />
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-px overflow-hidden border border-rule bg-rule md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          principles.map((p) => (
            <article class="bg-surface p-7">
              <h3 class="font-sans text-[1.05rem] font-semibold">{p.name}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2.5 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{p.body}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-6 font-mono text-[0.8rem] text-blue">
        <a href="/how-it-works/" class="hover:text-keyline">The machinery → How it works</a>
        <a href="/deployments/" class="hover:text-keyline">The public proof → Deployments</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
